[heading]About this mod[/heading]

[b]Travel Between Visited Traders[/b] adds a trader dialog option that lets players travel to traders they have already discovered.

Talking to a trader records that trader as visited. Later, the player can choose [b]Travel to a visited trader[/b] in trader dialog and teleport to an available destination.

[line]

[heading]Main features[/heading]

[list]
[*]Adds trader fast travel through dialog
[*]Works with previously visited traders only
[*]Supports English and Japanese
[*]Supports single-player and multiplayer
[*]Includes configurable trader-sharing behavior
[*]Briefly prepares unloaded destination areas before teleporting when needed
[*]Preserves compatibility with older save data
[/list]

[line]

[heading]Access modes[/heading]

Access modes are mainly for multiplayer. Single-player users can keep the default Personal mode and use the mod much like older versions.

[b]Default mode: Personal[/b]
If you do not change the config file, the mod uses Personal mode.

[b]Personal[/b]
Only traders visited by that specific player are available.

[b]Party[/b]
Traders visited by the player or by their current party members are available.

[b]Shared[/b]
Any trader visited by anyone in the active save or server data becomes available to everyone.

[line]

[heading]Which mode should I use?[/heading]

[list]
[*][b]Personal[/b] for individual unlocks or normal single-player use
[*][b]Party[/b] for co-op groups that should share discoveries only while grouped
[*][b]Shared[/b] for server-wide unlocks
[/list]

[line]

[heading]Installation[/heading]

Extract the [b]VisitedTraderTeleport[/b] folder into:

[quote]
7 Days To Die\Mods\VisitedTraderTeleport
[/quote]

The mod requires the vanilla [b]0_TFP_Harmony[/b] mod that ships with current 7 Days to Die versions.

[b]Anti-cheat should be disabled for this DLL mod.[/b]

[line]

[heading]Multiplayer[/heading]

Install this mod on both:

[list]
[*]The server
[*]Every client
[/list]

In multiplayer, the server controls:

[list]
[*]Which access mode is active
[*]Which visited traders each player may use
[*]Whether a requested teleport is allowed
[/list]

The client displays the destination list allowed by the server.

[line]

[heading]Upgrading from older versions[/heading]

Older versions stored visited trader data in:

[quote]
VisitedTraderTeleportVisited.txt
[/quote]

Current versions store new data in:

[quote]
VisitedTraderTeleportData.json
[/quote]

Upgrade behavior:

[list]
[*]Existing TXT data continues to load after upgrading
[*]Legacy TXT data is treated as a compatibility-wide shared pool so already available destinations do not suddenly disappear
[*]Legacy TXT data is not automatically rewritten into the new ownership-aware JSON schema
[*]New visits are recorded in the new JSON format
[*]The new format keeps trader destinations separate from player ownership, so changing between Personal, Party, and Shared later does not require resetting new-version data
[/list]

[b]Dedicated server note[/b]
Legacy data is read from the machine that owns the active save. Old TXT files that exist only on former clients are not transferred automatically.

[line]

[heading]Configuration[/heading]

Edit:

[quote]
7 Days To Die\Mods\VisitedTraderTeleport\Config\VisitedTraderTeleport.xml
[/quote]

Change:

[quote]
<AccessMode value="personal" />
[/quote]

to one of:

[list]
[*]<AccessMode value="personal" />
[*]<AccessMode value="party" />
[*]<AccessMode value="shared" />
[/list]

For multiplayer, edit the file on the server.

Restart the affected game process after changing the setting:

[list]
[*]Single-player: restart the game
[*]Multiplayer server: restart the dedicated server or host process
[/list]

[line]

[heading]Local testing option[/heading]

The config includes an advanced testing option:

[quote]
<TestRecordAllTradersOnVisit value="false" />
[/quote]

Leave this disabled for normal play.

If enabled, talking to any trader records all known traders for that player. These test destinations are saved two blocks in front of each trader's facing direction. This is mainly useful for local testing of unloaded-destination travel.

[line]

[heading]Notes[/heading]

[list]
[*]The current trader is not shown as a teleport destination
[*]If there are no valid destinations, only the normal "Never mind" response is shown
[*]Teleport destinations are based on previously recorded trader visits
[/list]
